          "label": "Quadratic factor",
          "inputProfile": "expression",
          "expected": "{{m2}}*x^2+({{mn}})*x+{{n2}}"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "Difference of cubes gives one linear and one quadratic factor.",
        "reasoning": [
          "Write {{m3}}x^3=({{m}}x)^3 and {{n3}}={{n}}^3.",
          "Use a^3-b^3=(a-b)(a^2+ab+b^2).",
          "The factors are {{m}}x-{{n}} and {{m2}}x^2+{{mn}}x+{{n2}}."
        ],
        "answerSummary": "Linear: {{m}}x-{{n}}; quadratic: {{m2}}x^2+{{mn}}x+{{n2}}."
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "Identify the two cube roots first; then apply the sign pattern of the difference-of-cubes identity."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "For a^3-b^3, the quadratic factor uses all positive terms: a^2+ab+b^2."
      ],
